& [VerbatimProductDirection]
  + "I want a Cantor for hosting a LLM, with something like a Needle or Needle 2 model running SOP, and then that running a SOP contract to load and run another LLM, so that the slim Cantor agent becomes the launch pad for another LLM, where we will host the larger Cantor, with a shared attention window they negotiate their shared perspective in inference. So Cantor will run a Cantor that runs the full system."
  + "get to a thick 5-hour slice now"

& [PreservedDependency]
  + published NHC-01 declares the outer host session process and model identity without observing a process or loading a model
  + published NHC-02 binds one proposed inner Cantor session and process lineage to the exact NHC-01 envelope with lineage_correspondence_only authority
  + the dependency plan selects NHC-03 inner model artifact admission loaded-instance identity and explicit model-loading authority before any launch plan

& [SelectedBoundedSurface]
  + form the smallest deterministic provider-free contract that binds one supplied inner-model artifact descriptor and one proposed loaded-instance identity to one exact validated NHC-02 envelope
  + distinguish artifact identity artifact admission load eligibility load authorization load attempt load completion and runtime observation so none can be inferred from another
  + require an exact content digest byte length format family selector provenance and policy references for the supplied artifact descriptor while treating every value as supplied and unobserved
  + require a proposed loaded-instance UUID configuration digest context ceiling and resource ceiling distinct from the outer model inner Cantor and process identities
  + make any positive model-loading authorization explicit bounded single-child single-artifact and consumable only by a later separately governed effect contract; compilation performs no load
  + retain artifact bytes file presence license truth malware safety provider compatibility memory fit runtime support and successful loaded state as unresolved unless separately evidenced

& [Delineation]
  + Needle or Needle 2 is a permitted opaque candidate selector, not an installed available compatible licensed safe or tested model claim
  + a SHA256-shaped supplied descriptor is not physical byte observation and artifact admission is not model loading
  + a proposed loaded-instance identity is not a loaded model, and model-loading authorization is not an attempt completion process launch provider call or inference event
  + NHC-04 launch planning NHC-05 custody NHC-06 negotiated shared attention NHC-07 provider-free integration NHC-08 live local models NHC-09 operator product and every remote deployment remain separate

